    {
      "id": 50,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        490,
        1060
      ],
      "size": [
        400,
        470
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 21,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note",
      "properties": {
        "text": ""
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "V2V STYLE SHIFT -- how this works\n\nThe whole source clip goes in as ONE guide clip on\nAddGuide at frame_idx 0. That is dense conditioning:\nevery output frame has a source row at its own time\ncoordinate, so motion and composition are held.\n\nDenoise stays at 1.00. The video is regenerated from\nnoise, which is what lets the style actually change and\nwhat produces NEW detail rather than sharpening what is\nalready there. Lowering denoise preserves the source's\nown look -- the thing you are trying to replace.\n\nGuide length must be on the 17k+5 grid (5, 22, 39, 56,\n73, 90...) and no longer than `length` on the H3 node.\nAddGuide crops down to the grid on its own, but it\nERRORS if the cropped clip is longer than the canvas.\n90 is used here because it is also on the audio clock\n(divisible by 3), so lip sync holds if you add speech.\n\nAddGuide centre-crops the guide to the canvas aspect.\nSet width/height to your source's aspect or you lose\nthe edges."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 51,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        1930,
        740
      ],
      "size": [
        460,
        560
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 22,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note",
      "properties": {
        "text": ""
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "WHY A DENSE GUIDE IGNORED THE PROMPT, AND THE FIX\n\nH3 mixes noise into every visual condition row, and the\namount is read from the conditioning:\n\n  # comfy/ldm/minimax/model.py:502\n  aug = payload.get(\"visual_cond_noise_aug\", 0.999)\n  if aug < 1.0:\n      r = aug * r + (1.0 - aug) * noise\n\nNOTHING in ComfyUI ever set that key -- not core, not\nthis pack -- so every render before H3GuideStrength ran\nat 0.999. Guide rows arrive 99.9% clean AND are labelled\nas finished (model.py:584, seg_t[\"cond\"]). Both say the\nsame thing: trust this row.\n\nRight for one reference image. Wrong for a guide clip\ncovering all 90 frames, which then fully specifies every\noutput frame. The first run of this workflow changed\nnothing for exactly that reason -- not a weak style\nsignal, an unarguable guide.\n\nTHE SWEEP, same seed, same clip:\n\n  visual 0.999  the old behaviour: output = input\n  visual 0.90   <-- start here (set now)\n  visual 0.70   looser; expect real style movement\n  visual 0.50   expect structure to start slipping\n\nFind where style appears and motion still holds. THEN\nadd the style LoRA on top, and only then reach for CFG.\n\nCAVEAT: _cond_video_rows walks keyframes AND references\ntogether, and seg_t sets \"cond\" and \"ref_img\" from the\nsame number. This dial cannot loosen a guide while\nleaving reference images alone. Fine here -- no refs.\n\nUNPROVEN at every value except 0.999."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 52,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        1470,
        780
      ],
      "size": [
        420,
        470
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 23,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note",
      "properties": {
        "text": ""
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "AUDIO -- why it is LOCKED, not passed through\n\nH3AudioLock replaces the AV latent's audio half with the\nreal encoded track and sets the sampler's mask to 0\nthere, so only video is generated. The mask is re-applied\nat EVERY denoise step, so the audio cannot drift.\n\nThat matters here because both streams share ONE packed\nsequence. The picture is generated against the real\nsoundtrack at every step, so mouths and motion answer to\nthe actual audio.\n\nSimply pasting the source audio over the output does NOT\ndo this: the model would generate its own audio track,\nlip-sync the video to THAT, and then you would replace it\nwith something else. Mismatched mouths.\n\nThe source audio is STILL passed straight to VideoCombine\nso the saved file is bit-exact rather than round-tripped\nthrough the audio VAE. The lock is for its effect on the\npicture.\n\nstrength 1.0 pins exactly. Lower lets the model\nreinterpret the track.\n\nIf the source audio is silence or useless room tone, set\nstrength to 0 -- there is nothing for the picture to\nanswer to."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
